# Implementation Plan - Crime Reporting and Public Safety Management System

## Goal Description
Build a full-stack web application for citizens to report crimes and police to manage them. The system will features a Node.js backend, MySQL database, vanilla HTML/CS/JS frontend, and a Python-based Naive Bayes classifier for crime categorization.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> This project requires a local MySQL server installation. The provided code will assume standard credentials (which should be configured in a `.env` file). Use the provided `schema.sql` to initialize the database.

> [!NOTE]
> The ML model will be a simple Python Flask service. Ensure Python is installed to run the ML component.

## Proposed Changes

### Database
#### [NEW] [schema.sql](file:///C:/Users/malip/.gemini/antigravity/brain/bd1f0466-b79d-49d3-a057-b2413a8b044e/database/schema.sql)
- Users Table: Stores citizen and admin credentials.
- CrimeReports Table: Stores complaint details, status, and ML classification.
- Evidence Table: Links to uploaded media.
- Remarks Table: History of admin updates.

### Machine Learning (Python)
#### [NEW] [ml_service.py](file:///C:/Users/malip/.gemini/antigravity/brain/bd1f0466-b79d-49d3-a057-b2413a8b044e/ml/ml_service.py)
- Flask app exposing `/predict` endpoint.
- Uses `scikit-learn` or custom Naive Bayes implementation for text classification.
- Includes a training endpoint or pre-trained model loading.

### Backend (Node.js/Express)
#### [NEW] [server.js](file:///C:/Users/malip/.gemini/antigravity/brain/bd1f0466-b79d-49d3-a057-b2413a8b044e/server/server.js)
- Main entry point. Setup middleware, database connection, and routes.
#### [NEW] [routes](file:///C:/Users/malip/.gemini/antigravity/brain/bd1f0466-b79d-49d3-a057-b2413a8b044e/server/routes/)
- `auth.js`: Login/Register logic.
- `reports.js`: CRUD for reports, file upload handling, and internal call to ML service.

### Frontend (HTML/CSS/JS)
#### [NEW] [client](file:///C:/Users/malip/.gemini/antigravity/brain/bd1f0466-b79d-49d3-a057-b2413a8b044e/client/)
- `index.html`: Landing page.
- `login.html`, `register.html`: Auth pages.
- `dashboard.html`: Main user interface (dynamic based on role).
- `report.html`: Complaint form.
- `css/style.css`: Custom styling.
- `js/app.js`: API interactions and DOM manipulation.

## Verification Plan
### Automated Tests
- None planned for this student-level project, but manual API testing with Postman/Curl.
### Manual Verification
- Start MySQL, create DB from schema.
- Start Python ML service.
- Start Node.js server.
- Register a user -> Login -> Submit Report (Verify ML tag) -> Admin Login -> Update Status.
